# A real team: the lead is asked for two teammates, and each one opens as a
# pane of the workspace, named and listed on the rail.
#
# This is the one scene that talks to the agent, because a team only exists
# once a lead has opened one. The prompt is short on purpose and the teammates
# are asked to report rather than to change anything in the project.
title lmux team
size 140 38
pre lmux kill --all
pre rm -rf .devcontainer
run lmux team . --nested
wait 8
frame 1.6
type Open two teammates: name the first api-review, ask it to describe internal/gateway, and name the second docs-pass, ask it to describe the README. Do not change any file.
enter
wait 25
frame 2.4
film 4 1.4
wait 20
frame 3
# The rail is open by now, with a row per teammate. Focusing it gives the keys
# below to the rail rather than to the lead.
keys M-[
wait 1.2
frame 1.4
# The shared task list of the team, and back to the rail.
keys t
wait 3
frame 2.6
keys q
wait 1.4
# The transcript of a teammate: what it was asked, what it answered, and the
# tools it called. The rows are the lead section, the lead, the teammates
# section and then the teammates, so three moves land on the first of them.
keys Down
wait 0.5
keys Down
wait 0.5
keys Down
wait 0.8
keys r
wait 3.5
frame 2.6
keys q
wait 1.4
frame 2
